MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1963640d94415114d8eb3f359d5b928b, type: 3}
  m_Name: Opening_DialogueData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueSO
  locationDialogue: Demon Lord Defeat
  dialogueLines:
  - characterName: 
    dialogueLine: 'For a hundred years, a shadow sat upon the throne of this land''s
      Life Tree, not the dark '
  - characterName: 
    dialogueLine: throne the old songs warn children about, but a throne all the
      same. A regional grief. A local dark.
  - characterName: 
    dialogueLine: They came from four corners of this land, a swordsman who never
      lost a duel, a priestess older than the kingdom's oldest maps, and an archer
      who could still an army's heartbeat with a single arrow.
  - characterName: 
    dialogueLine: They did not march against a king. Kings are for other stories,
      other wars, other heroes far from here.
  - characterName: 
    dialogueLine: They marched against the one who knelt to that king and ruled in
      his name, a Lord set over this soil, this tree, this people.
  - characterName: 
    dialogueLine: Beneath him, knights who had forgotten mercy. Beneath the knights,
      soldiers who had never known it.
  - characterName: 
    dialogueLine: And beneath all of them, small horrors that grew in the dark like
      weeds, spawn of a war none of them started.
  - characterName: 
    dialogueLine: It does not take a King to drown a country in a hundred years of
      night. It only takes the one left in charge of it.
  - characterName: 
    dialogueLine: They came because someone had to be last, the last blade drawn,
      the last prayer spoken, the last arrow loosed into the dark heart of a throne
      room that was never the highest throne at all.
  - characterName: 
    dialogueLine: And when the seal finally broke, and the Life Tree breathed again
      for the first time in a century... ...the world kept turning, the swordsman
      kept swinging, the priestess kept praying.
  - characterName: 
    dialogueLine: Only one of them was done.
  - characterName: 
    dialogueLine: What nobody wrote songs about, was what happened the next morning,
      to the one who quietly put his bow down.
